Translation patch: combinators taking functions or closures (misc/raw/*, io, value)

Change: `.ok_or_else(unexpected_buf_eof)`, `.map(Cow::Borrowed)`, `.map(Self::new)`, `.map(Either::Left)`, `.map(Const::new)`, `.map_err(|e| ..)`, `.map(|x| x as u64)`, `.copied().map(RawConst::new)` and similar become explicit `match`es (with `return Err(unexpected_buf_eof())` where they were followed by `?`).
Why: Aeneas fails on functions and constructors used as values ("Unimplemented": the `FnOnce` impl of a fn item/constructor) and does not model `ok_or_else`.
Behaviour: Identical: each `match` is the definition of the combinator; `unexpected_buf_eof()` is still only called on the error path.

